1. Pick up the motor from the component rack.
2. Place the gearbox on the assembly table.
3. Open the component storage cabinet.
4. Close the assembly workstation drawer.
5. Move the empty parts bin beside the assembly station.
6. Pick up the screwdriver from the tool rack.
7. Place the circuit board on the inspection table.
8. Move the tool cart to the assembly station.
9. Pick up the robot arm component and place it on the assembly table.
10. Open the storage cabinet and retrieve the sensor module.
11. Pick up the completed assembly and place it on the inspection station.
12. Retrieve the wrench from the tool rack and place it on the workbench.
13. Open the parts drawer and collect the fastener box.
14. Pick up the battery pack and place it beside the robot chassis.
15. Collect the inspection report and place it on the supervisor's desk.
16. Pick up the empty container and place it in the recycling area.
17. Go to the component rack, collect the motor, and deliver it to Assembly Station A.
18. Navigate to the tool room, retrieve the torque wrench, and place it on the workbench.
19. Go to the inspection station, collect the approved assembly, and deliver it to the packaging area.
20. Navigate to Storage Shelf B, retrieve the sensor module, and place it on the assembly table.
21. Go to the packaging station, collect the empty carton, and return it to storage.
22. Navigate to the assembly line, collect the unfinished robot chassis, and place it at the inspection station.
23. Go to the quality control desk, retrieve the inspection checklist, and deliver it to Assembly Station C.
24. Navigate to the battery storage area, collect the battery pack, and place it on the charging station.
25. If the component bin is empty, retrieve replacement components from the storage room; otherwise continue with the assembly station.
26. If the inspection table contains a rejected assembly, move it to the rework station; otherwise deliver the approved assembly to packaging.
27. If the tool cart is available, transport the components using it; otherwise carry the components individually.
28. If the assembly workstation drawer is open, close it before leaving the station.
29. If a motor is unavailable on Rack A, retrieve one from Rack B.
30. If the packaging area is full, place the completed assembly in the temporary storage area.
31. If the battery pack is fully charged, deliver it to Assembly Station B; otherwise return it to the charging station.
32. Carry the circuit board without touching its electronic contacts.
33. Transport the glass sensor module without dropping or tilting it.
34. Move the completed robot assembly without colliding with nearby equipment.
35. Place the heavy motor on the lower storage shelf without stacking it on fragile components.
36. Deliver the battery pack while keeping it upright.
37. Carry the tool tray without allowing any tools to fall.
38. Move the inspection equipment carefully without disconnecting its cables.
39. Collect the required components for a robot assembly from storage, arrange them on the assembly table, deliver the completed assembly to inspection, and return the unused components to storage.
40. Restock Assembly Station A by collecting motors, sensors, fasteners, and battery packs from storage, placing each item in its designated location, and returning to the tool room.
41. Inspect every assembly station for misplaced tools, empty component bins, unfinished assemblies, and open storage drawers, correct each issue, and report completion.
42. Prepare a workstation by placing the required tools on the workbench, arranging the components on the assembly table, positioning an empty parts bin, and ensuring the workstation is ready for production.
43. Collect all approved assemblies from the inspection station, transport them to the packaging area, organize the packaging materials, and return to the assembly line.
44. Prepare the factory for the next production shift by organizing component racks, returning tools to the tool room, clearing the workbenches, parking the tool cart, and closing all storage cabinets.
45. Inspect the factory floor for misplaced components, abandoned tools, blocked walkways, open storage cabinets, and unfinished assemblies, resolve each issue, and return to the supervisor's desk.
